WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:05.200
For one week in November, a game got better ten times.

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:07.200
Ten changes to its brain.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.000
Each one tested on hundreds of games.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Each one a measured gain.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Added together:

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:14.800
six and a half points.

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:21.600
Then all ten were measured at once, against the game as it had been a week before.

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.200
The gain was zero.

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:27.400
How can that be?

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:31.400
Here is every change the search tried in two weeks.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Two thousand six hundred and sixty-seven of them, each placed by how well it scored.

00:00:37.400 --> 00:00:44.200
And here is the curve you would get if not one of them did anything at all.

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.200
They are the same curve.

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:51.400
So when we kept the best of them, we were keeping the luckiest.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.800
And luck, measured again, goes home.

00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:01.600
Every measurement is a little signal, wrapped in a great deal of noise.

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:08.800
A machine that learns must tell the two apart, or it will teach itself its own good fortune.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:18.000
This is the story of one machine that learns to play a game, and of the borders it built against its own luck.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:23.000
This is how a game learns.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:25.400
Not by anyone's opinion of it.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.200
By playing itself, many thousands of times, and keeping only what survives.

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.400
Begin from far away.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.000
There are three territories.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.200
Main is the game as people play it:

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:41.600
its rules, its brain, its net.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:44.400
Nothing in main is changed by hand.

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:46.800
To the right, eight ordinary machines.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:55.600
They take the game as it is now, and play whole games, to measure one change to its brain at a time.

00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.400
Only what is proved better goes back.

00:01:58.400 --> 00:02:00.800
To the left, three graphics cards.

00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:08.400
They take the rules of the world, and grow a small neural net inside a fast copy of it.

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:12.000
Only a net the game itself credits goes back.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:12.800
Four arrows.

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:16.000
Everything that follows is the inside of them.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.600
Between the territories are borders, and each has its price.

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:26.200
From main to the fleet, the crossing is free:

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:28.600
to read is to change nothing.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.000
From the fleet to the line:

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:36.200
a gain that held on seeds the trial never saw, and every gate.

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.200
From the line to main:

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.000
a proof.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.400
The new game against the old, nine thousand six hundred games.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:45.800
And from the cards to main:

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.600
the game's own reading of the net.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.000
Twice.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.200
First, the brain's loop.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.000
Thirteen arrows.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.200
We will take them one at a time.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.800
Start where the game is.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:07.800
Every dial and switch of its brain, exactly as shipped, is read out of main.

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:09.400
Nothing changes by looking.

00:03:09.400 --> 00:03:15.400
But every question the fleet will ask is asked against this, and against nothing else.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:20.000
The search makes a guess.

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.200
One dial moved.

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.400
One switch flipped.

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:28.400
Only one, when it can, so that if the game gets better, we know why.

00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.200
A trial is a question, put plainly:

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.400
is the game better with this one change?

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.600
The answer costs games.

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:46.200
One hundred and fifty of them, on thirteen maps, each played twice on the same roll of the dice:

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.600
once with the change, once without.

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:50.200
Most guesses do nothing.

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.800
The first read exists to let them go cheaply.

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:03.200
A guess that looks good is read again, with more games and a higher bar each time.

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.800
But notice the trap.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:10.800
We chose it because it scored high, and part of any high score is luck.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:14.800
So it is sent where its luck must start over.

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:18.200
Fresh seeds.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:21.400
Games no trial has ever been measured on.

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.000
If the gain is real, it is still there.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.800
If it was luck, it is gone.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.600
Up to six such reads are pooled.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:32.600
What survives is a candidate:

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:35.400
something we now have reason to believe.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.000
Belief is not enough, because points do not show everything.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.400
So the gates ask three things.

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.800
Is the gain worth a generation?

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:50.400
Does every scenario the game must pass still pass?

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:56.000
And if it gives something up, does it gain enough to pay for it?

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:59.200
Then it becomes one commit, on the line.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.000
The line is a waiting room for one.

00:05:05.000 --> 00:05:08.600
The new game, complete, plays the old game, complete:

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.600
nine thousand six hundred games.

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:13.400
Ten times what any trial was given.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.800
And nothing else may join the line until this is decided.

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:24.800
If it leads by three of its own errors, it crosses.

00:05:24.800 --> 00:05:26.400
The commit becomes main.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:35.200
This is the only door by which the game's brain ever changes, and what goes through it is exactly what was measured.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:41.000
If it does not lead, it comes off.

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:43.400
This matters more than it seems.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:50.200
A block that is worth nothing, left in place, becomes the ground every later trial stands on.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.200
For one week in November, ten such blocks stood there.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:58.800
But refused is not forgotten.

00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:04.800
The trial goes back to the search, with everything that was ever read of it.

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:09.200
On another day, on other values, it may be asked again.

00:06:11.800 --> 00:06:13.800
There is a third ending.

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:19.000
A line can win on every map together, and still lose on one.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Twelve maps for, one against:

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.600
is that a gain?

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:25.400
It is not a question of arithmetic.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:29.400
So the process stops, and says so, with the numbers.

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:33.600
And a person answers.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:41.600
On the thirteenth of November the line stood nearly four points ahead, with one map of thirteen two points behind.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:42.800
Paul sent it.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.800
This is the one border held by a human hand.

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:52.200
Last, a ruler that does not move.

00:06:52.200 --> 00:06:59.000
Today's game against the game of three fixed days, on the same two thousand seeds, every day.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:03.000
A line can pass every gate and still stand still.

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.800
The yardstick is how we would know.

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:10.000
Now the net's loop.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:13.600
Nine arrows, and the same care at every border.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:17.800
Now the other loop.

00:07:17.800 --> 00:07:21.800
Three graphics cards are given the rules of the world:

00:07:21.800 --> 00:07:28.200
the speed of a tank, the reach of its gun, the pillboxes, the trees, the maze.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:32.200
From them each builds a fast copy of that world.

00:07:32.200 --> 00:07:37.400
A net is worth growing only in the world it will fight in.

00:07:40.000 --> 00:07:42.000
On each card, an island:

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:49.600
two thousand and forty-eight small nets, fighting the best of their own past, a hundred generations at a sitting.

00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:54.400
The best of them is examined against a ladder of earlier champions.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:58.000
Beat the top rung, and it is a milestone.

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:05.000
But the arena is a copy, and a copy can flatter.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:07.400
So the milestone leaves its card.

00:08:07.400 --> 00:08:14.200
Five thousand seven hundred and sixty-six numbers, carried to an ordinary machine, to play the real game:

00:08:14.200 --> 00:08:20.600
one hundred and ninety-two games as itself, and the same games as the net already shipped.

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:25.600
Sometimes the game says no, plainly.

00:08:25.600 --> 00:08:27.200
The arena admired it.

00:08:27.200 --> 00:08:28.800
The game did not.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:33.200
Then it must stop being the bar the cards climb toward.

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:40.400
It is no rung of the ladder, and an island refused three times running sends its champions nowhere.

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.000
Sometimes the game says yes.

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.000
And here is the temptation:

00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:48.200
to believe it.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:53.000
But in forty-four such readings, one will say yes by chance alone.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:09:00.600
So a yes earns only a second reading, three times as long, on seeds it was not chosen on.

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:07.200
If the second reading agrees, the net crosses into main.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.000
It is the only door by which the game's net ever changes.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:19.600
On the thirteenth of November a net called M 30 went through it, nearly two points better, and confirmed.

00:09:22.200 --> 00:09:24.600
And now the verdict comes home.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:34.600
The net the game credited, together with the champions of every island still in good standing, is sent back across the border, to every card.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.800
Not as a visitor.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:46.400
Until this day, a net from another card was only an opponent, and three cards grew three different nets.

00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:50.000
Now a migrant is written into the population itself.

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:52.800
If it ranks, it becomes a parent.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:54.800
The cards grow one net.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.200
And the island the game keeps refusing?

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.200
It is not switched off.

00:10:02.200 --> 00:10:05.800
It receives the better line, and breeds from it.

00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:10.200
It simply does not send, until the game stops saying no.

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:16.400
And one arrow more, where the two loops meet.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:21.400
One arrow joins the two loops.

00:10:21.400 --> 00:10:26.200
The shipped net plays in the very games that measure the brain.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:34.600
So the brain is tuned in a world that contains the net, and the net is grown under the brain's rules.

00:10:34.600 --> 00:10:37.400
Each is part of the other's weather.

00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:44.400
The same arrows, now with one real thing travelling over them.

00:10:44.400 --> 00:10:46.000
found on 5 November:

00:10:46.000 --> 00:10:51.200
+2.0 to +4.3 a seat, every time it was read its first read:

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:54.400
+4.29 a seat over every bar held out:

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:58.000
+3.46 +/- 0.54 09:09 the trade rule is changed:

00:10:58.000 --> 00:11:04.800
it gives up 0.44 kills, and gains enough to pay for it 10:40 on the line, alone.

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:10.800
The proof begins 12:57 proved, +3.91 +/- 0.11, and one map of thirteen reads under:

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.000
held, and silent 13:22 the flag is raised.

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.600
13:45 Paul sends it.

00:11:15.600 --> 00:11:16.800
It is main

00:11:19.400 --> 00:11:23.800
The same arrows, now with one real thing travelling over them.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:24.600
10 November:

00:11:24.600 --> 00:11:29.400
calber's island elects its champion at generation 290,500 read in the game:

00:11:29.400 --> 00:11:37.000
+2.28 +/- 0.98 over the shipped net, on 192 seeds its ship fails on a file size nobody updated.

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:40.200
Three days at the border, unread 13 November:

00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:43.800
shipped at 11:39, then checked on 576 fresh seeds:

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:45.000
+1.85 +/- 0.70.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:52.200
Confirmed the game's net returns to the cards and at 13:51 the first two migrants join calber's population

00:11:54.800 --> 00:12:00.000
Step back, and the two loops are one shape, drawn at every border.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:02.000
Something cheap makes a guess.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:06.000
Something honest measures it, on seeds the guess never saw.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:08.000
A rule, written down, decides.

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.200
One thing crosses.

00:12:09.200 --> 00:12:12.400
It is checked again on the other side.

00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:16.400
And the verdict returns to where the guess was made.

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:20.000
It is there between the fleet and the line.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:22.000
Between the line and main.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:24.400
And between the cards and main.

00:12:24.400 --> 00:12:26.000
A guess is cheap.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.600
A crossing is earned.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:30.800
And nothing that was learned is thrown away.

00:12:33.400 --> 00:12:37.400
If it is good, it is promoted, tested, and accepted.

00:12:37.400 --> 00:12:40.200
And what was learned goes back in.
